60,3,1,talk,Servas,,The candidates are before us. Let us weigh their needs against the hands and hours we actually possess.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Daisuke, the Microbiome Atlas fits perfectly! The repository is fast, and it’s a catalogue project that lasts forever!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Sakura, the Microbiome Atlas avoids the spectroscopy trap, but does it need the glasshouse space that is already full?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"- **Minako**: @Takumi, it relies on field sites, not glasshouses. The records show those sites lost seasons to weather, though.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Minako, field loss is a risk, but the Microbiome Atlas needs no scarce animal units or idle spectroscopy. It fits our current stability.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Servas, yes! And the free computing hours help with the sequence analysis. It’s the safest bet for us!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"- **Daisuke**: I hesitate. The closeout files show catalogue awards endure, but I fear we are ignoring the deeper mechanistic questions.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"-Takumi: @Daisuke, the mechanism projects stalled in the past. The Microbiome Atlas avoids those delays and uses the fast repository.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"- **Minako**: @Daisuke, the field site losses are a concern, but the indoor holding rooms remained stable. The risk is manageable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Daisuke, your caution is wise, but the hands we have now favor the catalogue. We must fund what can actually be completed.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Daisuke, but the data says the plain ones kept earning their keep! Let’s trust the records, not just the fancy ideas!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I understand your points. The records do show the catalogue endures, but I worry we are settling for safety over genuine discovery.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Daisuke, I hear you, but the spectroscopy suite is broken and the glasshouses are full. We can't fund a dream we can't execute.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, I respect your caution. But the infrastructure simply cannot support the other options right now. We must fund what is executable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: The vote is clear. We fund the Microbiome Atlas, matching our stable hands and fast repository to a lasting catalogue.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Sakura,,- **Sakura**: Yes! The Microbiome Atlas it is! I’m so happy we picked the one that actually works!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"- **Daisuke**: I accept the decision. The records support the choice, even if I miss the deeper questions.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,- **Takumi**: Agreed. The Microbiome Atlas is the only one we can actually finish without hitting a wall.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,- **Minako**: Agreed. The Microbiome Atlas is the only candidate that aligns with our current infrastructure and staffing reality.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
